From 95c99d5722e51f0d8de4107bfba369552620f151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:01:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure shared HTTP listener and worker
 diagnostics

Record local listener endpoints, public URL prefixes and worker counts under
distinct typed keys. Retain the original Info text, thread counts, options,
binding/validation predicates and failure returns. Capture socketpair's error
before constructing its event; never conflate a URL path with file.path or a
local listener with a remote peer.

Add an actual one-node fixture for public binding and numeric worker counts,
then four isolated invalid-option startups. Socketpair/bind exhaustion,
unhandled-request and listener-sharing rare branches are not newly forced.
The old WebSocket bind notice replaced by the incoming listen owner is left
for the canonical-source intake rather than duplicating that owner's work.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py 0.51.0):
  /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/http-listener-diagnostics.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/http-listener276-conversion.json --apply
  git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/httpserver.cpp

Source-only checkpoint pending combined native gate; preserve native252 seal.
Shared eCash owner, not Lotus consensus.
